1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,337
[♪ theme song playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

3
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:05,923
START DATING...

4
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,958
BETWEEN STEPS

5
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:43,794
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

6
00:00:43,877 --> 00:00:45,504
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

7
00:00:47,256 --> 00:00:49,258
[Youjin sobbing]

8
00:01:01,395 --> 00:01:02,521
[♪ emotional music playing]

9
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:03,605
Once...

10
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:06,984
I swallow something, I never spit it out.

11
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:13,156
I'd never spit it back out,
even if it burned me alive.

12
00:01:17,661 --> 00:01:19,204
There's no going back.

13
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:22,708
I have to see it through to the end.

14
00:01:27,254 --> 00:01:28,422
Do you still want this?

15
00:01:56,283 --> 00:01:57,284
Let's go.

16
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:51,254
[♪ music fades]

17
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:01,682
-[knocking at door]
-[Minjae] Youjin.

18
00:03:02,224 --> 00:03:03,225
Yes?

19
00:03:03,725 --> 00:03:04,726
What is it?

20
00:03:06,353 --> 00:03:09,314
[Minjae] I left your clothes by the door.

21
00:03:09,398 --> 00:03:11,191
Put them on when you come out.

22
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:12,359
I'll be in my room.

23
00:03:13,151 --> 00:03:14,152
Okay.

24
00:03:28,417 --> 00:03:29,626
[sighs]

25
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:31,253
EPISODE 6

26
00:03:31,336 --> 00:03:33,088
-Mmm... Done showering?
-Yeah.

27
00:03:33,171 --> 00:03:34,548
-Hot water working okay?
-Yeah.

28
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:36,049
You don't want to catch a cold.

29
00:03:36,133 --> 00:03:37,467
And your hair.

30
00:03:37,551 --> 00:03:39,553
Make sure you dry it completely.

31
00:03:39,636 --> 00:03:41,721
I dried most of it.

32
00:03:41,805 --> 00:03:42,806
-You did?
-Yeah.

33
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:43,890
Oh...

34
00:03:44,433 --> 00:03:45,892
Right, come, come here.

35
00:03:45,976 --> 00:03:47,060
Come here.

36
00:03:47,144 --> 00:03:48,228
Sit here.

37
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:49,938
[refrigerator door opens]

38
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,066
[refrigerator door closes]

39
00:03:55,402 --> 00:03:56,486
Drink this.

40
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:57,988
-It'll warm you up.
-Thank you.

41
00:03:59,865 --> 00:04:00,866
[Minjae mumbles]

42
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:16,506
Have some more. You need to warm up.

43
00:04:16,590 --> 00:04:17,966
-Hmm?
-[Youjin] Okay.

44
00:04:29,811 --> 00:04:30,812
[Minjae] It's on...

45
00:04:30,896 --> 00:04:31,897
-Huh?
-[Minjae] You got it on your face.

46
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:33,815
Mmm...

47
00:04:34,858 --> 00:04:36,318
Are you done?

48
00:04:36,401 --> 00:04:37,402
[Youjin] Yes.

49
00:04:40,405 --> 00:04:41,615
If you're done, let's go.

50
00:04:41,698 --> 00:04:42,949
What?

51
00:04:43,033 --> 00:04:46,286
I can't seem to get a taxi
because of the rain. This...

52
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:48,538
I don't mind staying the night here.

53
00:04:48,622 --> 00:04:49,623
[Minjae] Hmm?

54
00:04:51,041 --> 00:04:53,835
My family said I could sleep over tonight.

55
00:04:55,545 --> 00:04:59,674
That's because they thought
you'd be watching the meteor shower

56
00:04:59,758 --> 00:05:01,802
and studying with your labmates.

57
00:05:02,886 --> 00:05:05,722
You can't just go spending the night
at some guy's place.

58
00:05:05,806 --> 00:05:08,683
When did I ever say I was staying
at just some guy's place?

59
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:09,768
-[cellphone vibrates]
-What do you...

60
00:05:09,851 --> 00:05:12,229
We got one. Let's go.

61
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:13,772
-[Youjin] Huh?
-We got a taxi.

62
00:05:14,356 --> 00:05:15,357
Come on.

63
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:17,359
-But...
-Right, don't forget your clothes.

64
00:05:20,445 --> 00:05:21,446
[Youjin] But...

65
00:05:22,489 --> 00:05:23,657
Do you have everything?

66
00:05:25,617 --> 00:05:26,618
[Youjin] Hello.

67
00:06:22,424 --> 00:06:23,425
[Minjae] Aren't you getting out?

68
00:06:23,508 --> 00:06:25,510
[blinker ticking]

69
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:27,178
[seatbelt clicks]

70
00:06:27,262 --> 00:06:28,263
[Youjin] Have a good night.

71
00:06:38,523 --> 00:06:39,816
-What... hey.
-[Youjin exclaims]

72
00:06:40,442 --> 00:06:42,319
What if someone sees us?

73
00:06:42,402 --> 00:06:43,570
It's your neighborhood.

74
00:06:43,653 --> 00:06:45,655
Who's going to see us?
There's no one around.

75
00:06:45,739 --> 00:06:47,741
[indistinct chatter]

76
00:06:49,242 --> 00:06:50,243
[Minjae] There they are.

77
00:06:58,501 --> 00:06:59,502
Mmm...

78
00:07:00,170 --> 00:07:01,171
Bye.

79
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:03,673
Go on in.

80
00:07:04,341 --> 00:07:05,759
[Youjin] Call me when you get home.

81
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:07,886
Okay, will do.

82
00:07:10,722 --> 00:07:11,723
Wait.

83
00:07:12,682 --> 00:07:14,100
Youjin.

84
00:07:17,646 --> 00:07:21,900
How about we don't tell anyone
that we're dating for now?

85
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:31,159
I mean, I'm getting my PhD by the end
of this semester, so just until then.

86
00:07:31,242 --> 00:07:32,452
Just for the time being.

87
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,628
We don't have to keep it a secret, though.

88
00:07:43,672 --> 00:07:45,465
We don't have to, do we?

89
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:48,802
Well, that's not what I mean...

90
00:07:51,429 --> 00:07:53,181
So you want to tell everyone about it?

91
00:07:54,432 --> 00:07:56,643
Everyone in the lab?

92
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:59,813
Taeho, Chansoo, Hangyeol, and Kim Sejin?

93
00:08:02,774 --> 00:08:04,776
[dog barking in distance]

94
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:08,738
Let's just keep it from everyone else
for the time being.

95
00:08:12,075 --> 00:08:13,368
Hmm?

96
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:23,586
[sighs]

97
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:27,841
[grunts]

98
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:31,845
[breathing heavily]

99
00:08:32,637 --> 00:08:34,472
[coughs]

100
00:08:34,556 --> 00:08:36,099
[clears throat]

101
00:08:39,227 --> 00:08:40,645
[sniffles]

102
00:08:44,899 --> 00:08:46,401
[sighs, sniffles]

103
00:08:46,484 --> 00:08:47,485
[exhales]

104
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:55,410
[groans softly]

105
00:08:55,493 --> 00:08:56,619
I'm so tired.

106
00:08:57,454 --> 00:08:58,455
[sighs]

107
00:08:59,289 --> 00:09:01,291
[footsteps approaching]

108
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:07,630
[♪ comical music playing]

109
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:41,581
[Sejin] Oh...

110
00:09:41,664 --> 00:09:42,665
[Minjae] Hey.

111
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:44,542
-What?
-[Minjae] Huh?

112
00:09:45,794 --> 00:09:47,378
What are you doing here?

113
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:51,925
Well, you guys said
you'd be watching the stars here,

114
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:53,384
so I came to check on you.

115
00:09:53,468 --> 00:09:54,469
Why did you come up?

116
00:09:58,973 --> 00:10:00,183
[Sejin yawns]

117
00:10:00,266 --> 00:10:02,477
Well, we were waiting
to see the meteor shower...

118
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:03,770
[Minjae] Yeah.

119
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:06,439
[sighs] ...but then
it suddenly started pouring.

120
00:10:06,523 --> 00:10:08,775
Yeah, it came out of nowhere.

121
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:11,569
I was worried about you guys,
so I came over.

122
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:19,035
You can always catch the next one,
so don't be too disappointed.

123
00:10:20,078 --> 00:10:22,080
[Sejin] Well... I guess.

124
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:23,581
[Minjae] Yeah.

125
00:10:24,833 --> 00:10:27,001
And when you're done,
clean up after yourselves.

126
00:10:27,085 --> 00:10:28,419
Where are the trash bags?

127
00:10:28,503 --> 00:10:30,130
No, this isn't it.

128
00:10:30,213 --> 00:10:31,506
Where are the trash bags?

129
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:33,174
Leave it. I'll do it.

130
00:10:33,258 --> 00:10:36,219
Man, this is... Where are the trash bags?

131
00:10:36,302 --> 00:10:37,387
Just leave it.

132
00:10:39,889 --> 00:10:40,932
Right.

133
00:10:41,432 --> 00:10:42,684
[Minjae] What? What is it?

134
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:44,727
Where did Lim Youjin go?
Have you seen her?

135
00:10:44,811 --> 00:10:46,229
-Where did she go?
-[Minjae] Youjin?

136
00:10:46,312 --> 00:10:49,149
-She wasn't downstairs either.
-[Minjae] She left. She went home.

137
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,278
I saw her take a taxi earlier.

138
00:10:54,946 --> 00:10:56,072
She went home?

139
00:10:56,156 --> 00:10:59,576
Yeah, I mean...
It was just pouring earlier.

140
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:02,787
She probably figured she wouldn't
be able to see anything, and left.

141
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:04,372
Wow.

142
00:11:05,206 --> 00:11:07,458
If she was going,
she could've said something.

143
00:11:07,542 --> 00:11:10,503
She can't just slip out without a word.
What a little sneak.

144
00:11:10,587 --> 00:11:12,255
Seriously, she's such a weirdo.

145
00:11:12,839 --> 00:11:13,840
[Sejin sighs]

146
00:11:16,426 --> 00:11:18,386
Hey, Kim Sejin.

147
00:11:20,305 --> 00:11:22,015
I told you to quit it, didn't I?

148
00:11:23,558 --> 00:11:24,559
Didn't I?

149
00:11:27,353 --> 00:11:30,440
Why are you always
at each other's throats?

150
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:33,067
Why do you two have to fight
every time you're together?

151
00:11:34,235 --> 00:11:36,988
She's always picking fights
and getting on my nerves.

152
00:11:37,071 --> 00:11:40,033
Even if she starts it
and gets on your nerves,

153
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:42,160
just be patient and let it go.

154
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:43,244
[Sejin] Why should I?

155
00:11:43,328 --> 00:11:46,748
Why should I always have to be
the patient one and give in?

156
00:11:46,831 --> 00:11:49,125
Because, dude...

157
00:11:51,794 --> 00:11:53,254
You're a leader who's kinder,

158
00:11:54,756 --> 00:11:56,090
more understanding,

159
00:11:57,467 --> 00:11:59,219
and more generous than she is.

160
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:02,513
You...

161
00:12:04,307 --> 00:12:07,393
When you first joined our lab,
you have no idea how happy I was.

162
00:12:10,355 --> 00:12:14,442
I thought, "We have a really hardworking,
smart, and talented new member.

163
00:12:15,318 --> 00:12:19,322
Now I finally have a labmate
I can really trust and count on.

164
00:12:20,281 --> 00:12:24,202
The lab will be just fine without me."

165
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:27,080
You're just flattering me.

166
00:12:28,122 --> 00:12:29,707
We've got other senior members.

167
00:12:29,791 --> 00:12:32,585
Come on. Those... Those guys... [inhales]

168
00:12:32,669 --> 00:12:35,588
No matter how many times
I tell them, they never listen.

169
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:37,674
All they think about is screwing around.

170
00:12:39,384 --> 00:12:42,804
Just thinking about those guys
gives me an ulcer. You know that.

171
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:48,268
You see, Sejin, you're honestly
the only one I can trust and count on.

172
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:50,979
[Sejin sighs]

173
00:12:51,854 --> 00:12:55,400
And leaders are supposed to...

174
00:12:56,651 --> 00:12:58,194
I know you're smart.

175
00:12:58,278 --> 00:13:00,613
But when it comes to leadership,
heart beats brains.

176
00:13:01,739 --> 00:13:04,826
Kindness and generosity, you know?

177
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:08,329
Okay.

178
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:10,081
All right.

179
00:13:10,164 --> 00:13:12,583
I'm counting on you. Okay?

180
00:13:14,002 --> 00:13:15,837
[coughs]

181
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:17,964
-[sniffles] Oh man.
-Are you okay?

182
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:20,133
I keep feeling like I need to snee...

183
00:13:20,883 --> 00:13:22,677
[Minjae sneezes loudly, coughs]

184
00:13:24,762 --> 00:13:25,763
Jeez.

185
00:13:28,558 --> 00:13:29,559
Hey.

186
00:13:34,147 --> 00:13:35,857
That wasn't because of me, was it?

187
00:13:39,319 --> 00:13:40,820
[suppressed yell]

188
00:13:40,903 --> 00:13:41,904
I mean...

189
00:13:42,739 --> 00:13:45,491
-[Sejin whimpers]
-[Minjae] Hey, this...

190
00:13:45,575 --> 00:13:46,701
[Sejin groans]

191
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:48,786
[♪ gentle music playing]

192
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,082
[Minjae groans]

193
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:58,254
[grunts]

194
00:13:58,337 --> 00:14:00,882
[coughing]

195
00:14:03,718 --> 00:14:04,719
[groans]

196
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:07,972
[cellphone vibrates]

197
00:14:10,099 --> 00:14:11,100
[grunts]

198
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:15,438
[Youjin] <i>What are you up to?</i>

199
00:14:18,191 --> 00:14:19,192
[groans]

200
00:14:22,737 --> 00:14:23,738
[clicks tongue]

201
00:14:30,286 --> 00:14:31,370
[cellphone vibrates]

202
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,001
[Minjae] <i>Sleeping.</i>

203
00:14:41,172 --> 00:14:43,549
[Youjin] <i>Okay. You worked hard today.</i>

204
00:14:44,175 --> 00:14:45,676
<i>Sleep well. See you in my dreams.</i>

205
00:14:49,514 --> 00:14:50,515
[Minjae] <i>Yup.</i>

206
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:53,601
Come on.

207
00:14:53,684 --> 00:14:55,061
Write more than that.

208
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:09,659
[<i>♪ </i>music fades]

209
00:15:09,742 --> 00:15:10,743
[groans]

210
00:15:12,328 --> 00:15:13,704
[grunts]

211
00:15:21,546 --> 00:15:23,548
[♪ quirky music playing]

212
00:15:33,850 --> 00:15:36,352
[Youjin] <i>I totally slept in</i>
<i>because it's Sunday.</i>

213
00:15:36,435 --> 00:15:38,354
<i>Are you up? What are you doing?</i>

214
00:15:53,161 --> 00:15:54,203
<i>What are you doing?</i>

215
00:16:03,713 --> 00:16:05,798
Look at the time.
Why hasn't she come out yet?

216
00:16:07,383 --> 00:16:08,634
Hey, Youjin!

217
00:16:09,927 --> 00:16:11,345
Go wake her up.

218
00:16:11,429 --> 00:16:13,431
[Youseong] She'll come out
and eat when she's hungry.

219
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:14,515
[Miyoung] Leave her be.

220
00:16:14,599 --> 00:16:16,309
It's Sunday, so she can sleep in.

221
00:16:16,392 --> 00:16:18,394
But she has to eat something.

222
00:16:19,729 --> 00:16:21,731
She was reading till late last night.

223
00:16:24,317 --> 00:16:26,527
Sometimes it's hard to believe
she's my daughter.

224
00:16:27,195 --> 00:16:29,655
[chuckling] How could she
like studying so much?

225
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:33,492
[line ringing]

226
00:16:41,167 --> 00:16:42,168
[Minjae] <i>Hello?</i>

227
00:16:42,752 --> 00:16:43,920
Oh?

228
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:46,005
What took you so long to pick up?

229
00:16:46,797 --> 00:16:48,382
Didn't you get my message?

230
00:16:50,343 --> 00:16:55,932
[pharmacist] So take one of these
and two of these after every meal.

231
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:57,099
[Youjin] Okay.

232
00:16:59,352 --> 00:17:01,896
Do you know of any clinics
that are open around here?

233
00:17:01,979 --> 00:17:03,522
I couldn't find any online.

234
00:17:03,606 --> 00:17:04,690
Uh...

235
00:17:04,774 --> 00:17:06,192
I'm not sure.

236
00:17:06,275 --> 00:17:09,695
But if these don't work,
I'd recommend they go to the ER.

237
00:17:11,197 --> 00:17:12,740
I see. Thank you.

238
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:17,245
[doorbell rings]

239
00:17:22,667 --> 00:17:23,668
Mmm...

240
00:17:24,543 --> 00:17:29,382
-[coughing]
-[doorbell rings]

241
00:17:36,639 --> 00:17:38,182
[door lock chimes]

242
00:17:38,266 --> 00:17:39,267
Oh?

243
00:17:40,476 --> 00:17:41,894
[Sejin] What is it this time?

244
00:17:42,478 --> 00:17:44,105
You come here pretty often, huh?

245
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:47,692
[Youjin] I don't come here often.

246
00:17:48,276 --> 00:17:51,362
Well, I heard he's sick, so I wanted
to get him some meds and stuff.

247
00:17:51,445 --> 00:17:53,281
[Sejin] Ah... Meds.

248
00:17:54,865 --> 00:17:56,951
I already got him some.

249
00:18:02,248 --> 00:18:03,249
[door lock chimes]

250
00:18:03,958 --> 00:18:05,835
Hey, he's asleep. Don't wake him up.

251
00:18:07,003 --> 00:18:09,088
I said he's asleep.
You shouldn't wake him up.

252
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:10,673
Hey, move.

253
00:18:10,756 --> 00:18:12,008
Get out of my way.

254
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:15,469
[weakly] Hey, what's going on? What's up?

255
00:18:15,970 --> 00:18:17,054
I said, move!

256
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:20,683
Minjae, are you okay?

257
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:22,059
[mumbles] I'm okay, I'm okay.

258
00:18:22,143 --> 00:18:23,144
[Youjin] My goodness.

259
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:25,771
Hey, you're disturbing his sleep--

260
00:18:25,855 --> 00:18:26,939
Hey, stop, be quiet.

261
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:29,692
[Youjin] Uh... Hold on.

262
00:18:32,028 --> 00:18:33,029
[clicks]

263
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:35,281
[digital beeps]

264
00:18:35,364 --> 00:18:36,365
[softly in English] Thank you.

265
00:18:37,033 --> 00:18:38,951
[in Korean] I said I was fine.
Why did you come?

266
00:18:39,035 --> 00:18:40,828
Because I was worried.

267
00:18:41,412 --> 00:18:42,788
[light thud]

268
00:18:49,962 --> 00:18:51,047
[Sejin] Here.

269
00:18:51,672 --> 00:18:54,550
The porridge is ready,
so have some and then take your meds.

270
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:57,845
You didn't have to come. It's just a cold.

271
00:18:58,387 --> 00:18:59,555
Did you go to the doctor?

272
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:02,058
It's just a cold. No need to see a doctor.

273
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:04,602
I'll just take these meds
from the drugstore. I'm fine.

274
00:19:06,062 --> 00:19:09,190
I made it with equal parts milk and water.

275
00:19:09,273 --> 00:19:10,691
It's our family secret.

276
00:19:10,775 --> 00:19:11,776
[Minjae] Okay.

277
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:14,070
Thanks for making it.

278
00:19:14,737 --> 00:19:16,072
[Youjin] Here. Try some.

279
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:18,240
Wait.

280
00:19:19,408 --> 00:19:20,409
[Minjae] Why?

281
00:19:20,493 --> 00:19:21,911
What do you think you're doing?

282
00:19:22,578 --> 00:19:23,579
[Youjin] What?

283
00:19:27,208 --> 00:19:28,584
This is my porridge.

284
00:19:29,377 --> 00:19:30,795
Why are you doing this?

285
00:19:32,004 --> 00:19:33,381
[Youjin] What do you mean, my porridge?

286
00:19:33,464 --> 00:19:36,008
Why are you taking credit
for the porridge I made?

287
00:19:37,677 --> 00:19:40,721
-Go make your own porridge.
-[Minjae coughs]

288
00:19:42,056 --> 00:19:43,474
[Youjin] Jeez. Just you wait.

289
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:44,558
Have some.

290
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:47,311
Hey, guys, you guys
are giving me a headache.

291
00:19:47,395 --> 00:19:48,396
Seriously, stop.

292
00:19:48,479 --> 00:19:50,731
Eat this porridge and take the meds.

293
00:19:50,815 --> 00:19:54,443
Hey, you better not eat a single spoonful
of Kim Sejin's porridge, or else.

294
00:19:54,527 --> 00:19:56,654
[sighs] Or what would you do, exactly?

295
00:19:56,737 --> 00:19:58,572
-[Minjae softly] I'm cold.
-[Youjin sighs heavily]

296
00:19:58,656 --> 00:19:59,990
Look, Kim Sejin.

297
00:20:00,074 --> 00:20:02,660
Try all you want,
but you're never going to beat me.

298
00:20:02,743 --> 00:20:03,744
[Sejin chuckles softly]
What are you saying?

299
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:05,746
I'm not like you.

300
00:20:06,372 --> 00:20:07,707
Minjae and I are--

301
00:20:07,790 --> 00:20:08,791
[Minjae] Youjin.

302
00:20:11,127 --> 00:20:12,503
You see,

303
00:20:12,586 --> 00:20:14,505
-Minjae and I are...
-[Minjae coughing] Youjin.

304
00:20:16,716 --> 00:20:19,510
-We started--
-[doorbell rings]

305
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:20,886
[Minjae sighing] God, who is it now?

306
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:25,725
[doorbell rings]

307
00:20:25,808 --> 00:20:26,934
[Minjae] Who is it?

308
00:20:27,977 --> 00:20:28,978
Huh?

309
00:20:30,521 --> 00:20:32,189
[whispering] Should we just
not open the door?

310
00:20:32,815 --> 00:20:33,816
[Youjin] Yeah.

311
00:20:37,111 --> 00:20:38,112
[door lock chimes]

312
00:20:39,530 --> 00:20:40,531
[Seohyun] Oh?

313
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:42,408
You guys were here too?

314
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:43,492
-Hello.
-[Youjin] Hello.

315
00:20:43,576 --> 00:20:44,577
[Seohyun] Where's Minjae?

316
00:20:45,161 --> 00:20:46,203
Are you okay?

317
00:20:46,287 --> 00:20:48,080
[Minjae] What are you doing here?

318
00:20:48,706 --> 00:20:50,750
-Of course I'm here. You're sick.
-[door lock chimes]

319
00:20:50,833 --> 00:20:51,834
[Minjae] I'm fine.

320
00:20:52,376 --> 00:20:54,462
[Seohyun] I got you some abalone porridge.
Have some.

321
00:20:54,545 --> 00:20:56,213
-[Minjae coughs] These guys...
-[Seohyun] Here.

322
00:20:56,714 --> 00:20:58,466
I just bought it, so it's still warm.

323
00:20:58,549 --> 00:21:00,843
Look, it's not that serious. I'm fine.

324
00:21:00,926 --> 00:21:04,221
[Seohyun] I mean, who catches a cold
in the middle of summer?

325
00:21:04,305 --> 00:21:06,474
How'd you come down with a cold
all of a sudden?

326
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:11,187
It's sweet of you kids to come check
on your lab lead when he's sick.

327
00:21:11,729 --> 00:21:14,106
I can take care of him, so you can go now.

328
00:21:14,190 --> 00:21:16,442
Uh... I don't mind
staying a little longer.

329
00:21:17,109 --> 00:21:18,486
[Seohyun] It's okay. Go home.

330
00:21:18,569 --> 00:21:20,613
You have to work tomorrow.
Go get some rest.

331
00:21:21,113 --> 00:21:23,032
You should go too. You have work tomorrow.

332
00:21:23,115 --> 00:21:24,617
[Seohyun]
I'm sleeping over.

333
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:26,535
-What?
-[Seohyun] I can go to work from here.

334
00:21:27,161 --> 00:21:29,288
It's sad being alone when you're sick.

335
00:21:30,706 --> 00:21:32,958
Me too. I can stay the night here too.
[chuckles softly]

336
00:21:33,042 --> 00:21:35,294
Yeah, I was going to stay with him too.

337
00:21:35,377 --> 00:21:37,087
I live closest to here.

338
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:38,881
[Seohyun] Huh?

339
00:21:39,465 --> 00:21:41,133
But he's got me. Why would you guys?

340
00:21:42,635 --> 00:21:44,595
Because he's got me too.

341
00:21:45,888 --> 00:21:46,972
[Sejin] Still...

342
00:21:47,723 --> 00:21:50,976
I'm a guy, so... [chuckles]

343
00:21:51,060 --> 00:21:52,645
Hey, who cares if you're a guy?

344
00:21:53,145 --> 00:21:54,855
[Minjae coughs]

345
00:21:54,939 --> 00:21:57,149
Minjae is most comfortable around me.

346
00:21:57,650 --> 00:21:58,651
Wait.

347
00:21:59,819 --> 00:22:01,737
He feels comfortable around me too. Right?

348
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:04,406
[Sejin] We're both guys.

349
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:07,785
You don't feel comfortable
around two women, do you?

350
00:22:07,868 --> 00:22:09,870
[♪ comical music playing]

351
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:17,753
[♪ music stops]

352
00:22:17,837 --> 00:22:20,422
God, Park Minjae, always so darn stubborn.

353
00:22:21,131 --> 00:22:23,259
We come to check on him,
and he acts like this?

354
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:25,719
Looks like he's really not feeling well.

355
00:22:28,389 --> 00:22:29,723
I'll get going then.

356
00:22:29,807 --> 00:22:31,559
Okay. Bye.

357
00:22:33,853 --> 00:22:35,563
What are you looking at? Jeez.

358
00:22:37,439 --> 00:22:39,024
I'll get going too.

359
00:22:39,859 --> 00:22:41,360
Are you taking the subway?

360
00:22:42,111 --> 00:22:43,696
I can drop you off at the station.

361
00:22:44,196 --> 00:22:45,197
[Youjin] Well...

362
00:22:45,281 --> 00:22:47,616
-[footsteps receding]
-[♪ gentle music playing]

363
00:23:49,261 --> 00:23:51,263
[♪ music fades]

364
00:23:51,347 --> 00:23:53,057
Don't you think it's a bit strange?

365
00:23:53,766 --> 00:23:55,517
Why would he just kick us out?

366
00:23:57,853 --> 00:23:59,897
He's definitely keeping something from us.

367
00:24:02,107 --> 00:24:04,026
I think he's seeing a girl.

368
00:24:05,027 --> 00:24:06,362
[Youjin] Huh?

369
00:24:06,445 --> 00:24:07,446
[Seohyun] But who could it be?

370
00:24:07,988 --> 00:24:09,990
I don't think he had a blind date, though.

371
00:24:10,074 --> 00:24:11,367
Who could it be?

372
00:24:12,451 --> 00:24:14,453
Could it be...

373
00:24:15,579 --> 00:24:16,872
that woman with the Mercedes?

374
00:24:17,873 --> 00:24:19,124
[Seohyun] Hmm?

375
00:24:19,208 --> 00:24:21,669
The woman Kim Sejin saw outside his place.

376
00:24:21,752 --> 00:24:23,963
She drove a white Mercedes
and was really pretty.

377
00:24:24,046 --> 00:24:26,840
[chuckling softly] Oh, that.

378
00:24:28,384 --> 00:24:29,843
No.

379
00:24:29,927 --> 00:24:31,804
No, she can't be...

380
00:24:32,638 --> 00:24:33,973
They're nothing like that.

381
00:24:35,182 --> 00:24:36,433
Didn't Minjae tell you?

382
00:24:38,644 --> 00:24:39,645
No.

383
00:24:40,604 --> 00:24:41,855
Really?

384
00:24:41,939 --> 00:24:46,068
Well, if he didn't want to tell you,
there must've been a good reason.

385
00:24:52,199 --> 00:24:55,285
Looks like you know
everything about Minjae.

386
00:24:55,369 --> 00:24:57,037
You two must be really close.

387
00:24:57,121 --> 00:24:58,122
[Seohyun] Yeah.

388
00:24:58,998 --> 00:25:01,333
We go all the way back
to high school, so...

389
00:25:03,585 --> 00:25:06,255
I heard you're Minjae's first love.

390
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:08,507
[Seohyun chuckles]

391
00:25:10,050 --> 00:25:11,760
[Youjin] Then how come
you two never dated?

392
00:25:12,469 --> 00:25:14,471
That's not true. We used to date.

393
00:25:15,472 --> 00:25:16,640
You two used to date?

394
00:25:16,724 --> 00:25:18,809
[Seohyun] Yeah, for a little over a month.

395
00:25:21,061 --> 00:25:22,312
What, a month?

396
00:25:22,396 --> 00:25:24,565
That doesn't count as dating.

397
00:25:25,482 --> 00:25:27,735
No, you weren't really together.

398
00:25:27,818 --> 00:25:29,194
If that's considered dating,

399
00:25:29,278 --> 00:25:31,488
then there's no one on earth
who hasn't dated.

400
00:25:31,572 --> 00:25:33,741
Everyone's dated. Everyone.

401
00:25:33,824 --> 00:25:34,825
Am I wrong?

402
00:25:34,908 --> 00:25:36,326
It just doesn't make any sense.

403
00:25:37,578 --> 00:25:39,538
What do you mean,
it doesn't make any sense?

404
00:25:39,621 --> 00:25:43,876
If a man and a woman
held hands and kissed,

405
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:45,711
that means they were dating.

406
00:25:54,678 --> 00:25:56,680
[indistinct chatter]

407
00:25:57,931 --> 00:25:59,808
[sniffles, coughs]

408
00:26:07,107 --> 00:26:08,108
[groans softly]

409
00:26:09,443 --> 00:26:13,322
I also think high school first-love
is childish and lame, you know?

410
00:26:13,906 --> 00:26:15,240
It's all in the past anyway.

411
00:26:15,324 --> 00:26:16,492
It doesn't mean anything.

412
00:26:17,701 --> 00:26:19,119
And Kim Sejin.

413
00:26:19,203 --> 00:26:20,621
He's such a sycophant. Okay?

414
00:26:20,704 --> 00:26:22,372
He's a crazy little suck-up.

415
00:26:22,956 --> 00:26:25,125
And why do I even have
to compete with him?

416
00:26:25,209 --> 00:26:26,460
Park Minjae is mine anyway.

417
00:26:27,669 --> 00:26:29,671
[Jihoon] He's everyone's sweetheart,
as they say.

418
00:26:30,506 --> 00:26:33,717
Exactly. He's so nice to everyone but me.

419
00:26:33,801 --> 00:26:36,011
[Jihoon] If you know that,
why even compete with them?

420
00:26:37,054 --> 00:26:38,055
That's my point.

421
00:26:38,138 --> 00:26:40,557
Why on earth should I compete
with these people? Why?

422
00:26:40,641 --> 00:26:43,185
[Jihoon] Exactly. Why compete?

423
00:26:43,268 --> 00:26:44,812
I mean, yeah!

424
00:26:44,895 --> 00:26:47,231
Why do I have to compete with them?
What for?

425
00:26:47,314 --> 00:26:50,317
[Jihoon] Exactly.
So why compete with them?

426
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:53,112
Exactly. Why do I have
to compete with them?

427
00:26:56,198 --> 00:26:57,199
Monkey.

428
00:27:00,953 --> 00:27:02,913
Just take my class for one semester.

429
00:27:02,996 --> 00:27:05,249
All your problems
with life and love will be gone.

430
00:27:07,668 --> 00:27:08,669
Okay?

431
00:27:09,837 --> 00:27:11,505
-You sound like a snake oil salesman.
-[Jihoon chuckles softly]

432
00:27:11,588 --> 00:27:13,799
Yeah, I'm trying to win you over like one.

433
00:27:16,885 --> 00:27:19,847
If we'd made it official from the start
that we were dating,

434
00:27:19,930 --> 00:27:21,974
none of this would've happened.

435
00:27:22,057 --> 00:27:23,934
So, what is it you want to do, exactly?

436
00:27:25,227 --> 00:27:27,229
I'll tell him
to make it official, obviously.

437
00:27:28,188 --> 00:27:29,565
What if he doesn't want to?

438
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:30,691
Then?

439
00:27:31,817 --> 00:27:32,818
Then...

440
00:27:33,694 --> 00:27:34,987
we'll break up, I guess.

441
00:27:35,070 --> 00:27:37,072
Good. You got your answer. Now go.

442
00:27:37,155 --> 00:27:38,282
You're distracting me.

443
00:27:41,827 --> 00:27:42,828
[Minjae] Oh...

444
00:27:43,704 --> 00:27:45,122
[groans]

445
00:27:45,205 --> 00:27:46,290
Goodness.

446
00:27:46,915 --> 00:27:48,041
-Minjae.
-[Minjae] Yes?

447
00:27:48,125 --> 00:27:49,918
Want me to massage your shoulders?

448
00:27:50,002 --> 00:27:52,087
[Minjae] No, that's okay. I'm fine.

449
00:27:52,170 --> 00:27:53,171
Just a little.

450
00:27:53,255 --> 00:27:55,048
[Minjae] No, I'm fine.
I can use this. [groans]

451
00:27:55,132 --> 00:27:59,094
I used to give all the older members
of my family massages.

452
00:27:59,177 --> 00:28:01,722
-Oh boy.
-That's how I earned my allowance.

453
00:28:01,805 --> 00:28:02,806
[Minjae] Oh...

454
00:28:02,890 --> 00:28:03,891
-[Sejin grunts]
-[Minjae groans]

455
00:28:03,974 --> 00:28:04,975
[door opens]

456
00:28:05,058 --> 00:28:06,226
That's nice.

457
00:28:06,310 --> 00:28:07,644
-[door closes]
-[Minjae sighs in relief]

458
00:28:08,854 --> 00:28:11,023
[Minjae moaning]

459
00:28:14,109 --> 00:28:16,069
-[Sejin] Here?
-[Minjae groans]

460
00:28:18,864 --> 00:28:19,865
Hi, Youjin.

461
00:28:19,948 --> 00:28:21,742
-Hey.
-[Minjae sighs in relief]

462
00:28:23,577 --> 00:28:25,245
-You're really good.
-[Sejin grunts]

463
00:28:25,329 --> 00:28:27,039
[Minjae] Gosh, that really hits the spot.

464
00:28:28,040 --> 00:28:30,125
[Minjae groans in relief]

465
00:28:33,462 --> 00:28:35,797
Well, Sejin was just giving me a massage

466
00:28:35,881 --> 00:28:37,758
because I said my shoulders were hurting.

467
00:28:37,841 --> 00:28:39,968
I don't see what's wrong with that.

468
00:28:41,219 --> 00:28:43,180
I'm going to tell Kim Sejin everything.

469
00:28:43,263 --> 00:28:44,264
That we're dating.

470
00:28:45,223 --> 00:28:46,725
We already talked about this.

471
00:28:48,268 --> 00:28:49,937
I heard about Seohyun too.

472
00:28:51,563 --> 00:28:52,940
You two used to date?

473
00:28:55,984 --> 00:28:59,446
From now on, don't meet up with her alone
or have her over at your place.

474
00:28:59,529 --> 00:29:01,281
Don't go over to hers, either.

475
00:29:04,493 --> 00:29:07,079
I can't promise that.

476
00:29:09,081 --> 00:29:10,499
I mean, when she said we dated,

477
00:29:11,375 --> 00:29:14,336
all that happened
was we joked about dating

478
00:29:14,419 --> 00:29:16,296
if we ended up at the same college.

479
00:29:17,297 --> 00:29:19,383
And even then, it didn't last a month.

480
00:29:19,466 --> 00:29:21,343
It was really nothing.

481
00:29:22,469 --> 00:29:23,804
I heard you kissed too.

482
00:29:25,347 --> 00:29:27,265
That was barely a kiss.

483
00:29:27,349 --> 00:29:29,685
She's talking about the time
during a drinking game.

484
00:29:30,519 --> 00:29:33,480
I didn't feel a thing,
and I don't even remember it.

485
00:29:35,732 --> 00:29:37,025
This is really unfair.

486
00:29:37,109 --> 00:29:38,402
You're my first, I swear.

487
00:29:42,572 --> 00:29:44,825
You were pretty good
for your first time, though.

488
00:29:44,908 --> 00:29:45,909
What...

489
00:29:46,910 --> 00:29:48,161
You were better than...

490
00:29:49,913 --> 00:29:51,123
What about you? I bet...

491
00:29:51,832 --> 00:29:55,794
you kissed plenty
of other guys too, right?

492
00:29:56,712 --> 00:29:58,088
[Youjin scoffs]

493
00:29:58,171 --> 00:30:00,507
Yes, tons of times.

494
00:30:01,383 --> 00:30:03,176
I've dated tons of guys.

495
00:30:03,260 --> 00:30:05,345
Kissing, making out, and everything else.

496
00:30:05,429 --> 00:30:06,847
I've done it all tons of times.

497
00:30:09,016 --> 00:30:10,642
Everything else?

498
00:30:13,478 --> 00:30:15,981
But that's all in the past.

499
00:30:16,690 --> 00:30:19,443
I'm not in touch with any of them anymore.
I've cut all ties.

500
00:30:21,611 --> 00:30:24,531
I'm not saying
you should never see her again.

501
00:30:24,614 --> 00:30:28,035
You just can't meet up with her alone
or have her over at your place.

502
00:30:29,703 --> 00:30:31,079
You can't even do that for me?

503
00:30:33,707 --> 00:30:35,125
No, I can't.

504
00:30:35,834 --> 00:30:36,835
[Youjin] Why not?

505
00:30:38,211 --> 00:30:40,630
Like I said, she's my best friend.

506
00:30:40,714 --> 00:30:43,383
Your girlfriend
should be your best friend. Me.

507
00:30:46,428 --> 00:30:48,638
Hey, the professor wants to see me.
I have to go.

508
00:30:49,222 --> 00:30:51,558
So you're okay with not seeing me anymore?

509
00:30:55,479 --> 00:30:57,105
Are you okay with not seeing me?

510
00:30:59,483 --> 00:31:01,318
Do you realize what you're saying?

511
00:31:03,195 --> 00:31:05,238
Of course I do. You think I don't?

512
00:31:13,330 --> 00:31:14,664
Okay. Fine.

513
00:31:16,708 --> 00:31:17,918
[Youjin] What do you mean, fine?

514
00:31:18,001 --> 00:31:19,961
That you can't see me anymore.

515
00:31:21,338 --> 00:31:22,339
I get it.

516
00:31:25,550 --> 00:31:26,551
[grunts]

517
00:31:30,472 --> 00:31:32,349
What if I can't see her anymore?

518
00:31:33,141 --> 00:31:36,269
I'm going to nip those nasty little games
in the bud. Jeez.

519
00:31:44,820 --> 00:31:47,155
[Hangyeol] Move it forward first.

520
00:31:52,285 --> 00:31:53,411
Now backward.

521
00:31:55,247 --> 00:31:56,248
To the right.

522
00:31:59,084 --> 00:32:00,085
To the left.

523
00:32:01,586 --> 00:32:02,587
Now, to the right.

524
00:32:08,635 --> 00:32:11,263
-Are we done?
-Yeah, we're done.

525
00:32:11,346 --> 00:32:13,890
How do the peak torque
and left-right balance look?

526
00:32:13,974 --> 00:32:15,016
They're all good.

527
00:32:15,100 --> 00:32:16,101
-Yeah?
-Yes.

528
00:32:16,184 --> 00:32:18,270
Don't we need to work
on posture control too?

529
00:32:19,646 --> 00:32:20,647
[Minjae] Yeah.

530
00:32:20,730 --> 00:32:23,358
Guys, we need the results
by the end of next month.

531
00:32:23,441 --> 00:32:24,818
Okay?

532
00:32:24,901 --> 00:32:26,069
That's going to be tight.

533
00:32:32,534 --> 00:32:33,743
Good work, guys.

534
00:32:34,286 --> 00:32:35,412
Let's call it a day.

535
00:32:35,495 --> 00:32:36,913
[flushing]

536
00:32:41,793 --> 00:32:43,795
[cellphone vibrates]

537
00:32:47,132 --> 00:32:49,718
[Minjae] <i>Go ahead and wait for me</i>
<i>at my place. I'll be there soon.</i>

538
00:32:57,475 --> 00:32:58,894
[Youjin] <i>So you promise?</i>

539
00:33:01,271 --> 00:33:02,522
[Minjae] <i>What promise?</i>

540
00:33:02,606 --> 00:33:03,815
<i>Don't start with me.</i>

541
00:33:11,031 --> 00:33:13,033
[Youjin] <i>What if Kim Sejin is there?</i>

542
00:33:14,451 --> 00:33:16,369
[Minjae] <i>He went to Daejeon</i>
<i>for a family gathering.</i>

543
00:33:19,414 --> 00:33:21,249
[Youjin] <i>I don't know the passcode</i>
<i>to your place.</i>

544
00:33:24,961 --> 00:33:26,129
[Minjae] <i>The day we first met.</i>

545
00:33:27,589 --> 00:33:29,591
-[♪ gentle music playing]
-[giggles]

546
00:33:42,562 --> 00:33:43,855
[door lock chimes]

547
00:33:44,606 --> 00:33:45,607
[door opens]

548
00:33:53,615 --> 00:33:54,616
[door lock chimes]

549
00:35:05,437 --> 00:35:08,440
SLAM DUNK

550
00:35:09,107 --> 00:35:11,109
[♪ gentle music continues playing]

551
00:36:33,608 --> 00:36:35,610
[♪ music fades]

552
00:36:36,695 --> 00:36:38,988
[Jaehong] Yeah.
Spring brides are always the prettiest.

553
00:36:39,072 --> 00:36:41,116
-You picked a good date.
-[Seohyun chuckles]

554
00:36:41,199 --> 00:36:42,200
Congratulations.

555
00:36:42,283 --> 00:36:45,286
Yeah, thank you. [chuckles]

556
00:36:45,370 --> 00:36:47,038
It's at the wedding hall on campus.

557
00:36:47,122 --> 00:36:48,164
You'll come, right?

558
00:36:48,248 --> 00:36:50,959
Distance doesn't matter.
Of course I'll come.

559
00:36:51,042 --> 00:36:54,421
She's my favorite, you know, student.

560
00:36:54,504 --> 00:36:56,798
[chuckles softly] You promise?

561
00:36:56,881 --> 00:36:59,008
[Jaehong] Of course. See?

562
00:36:59,092 --> 00:37:01,803
Everyone else is finding someone
and settling down.

563
00:37:01,886 --> 00:37:03,513
Park Minjae, what's wrong with you?

564
00:37:03,596 --> 00:37:06,307
Me? Why are you suddenly
making this about me? [chuckles]

565
00:37:06,391 --> 00:37:09,519
Wouldn't it be great to meet someone
and take her to the States?

566
00:37:10,395 --> 00:37:12,313
Do you know anyone
you could set him up with?

567
00:37:12,397 --> 00:37:15,233
[sighs] He's really picky, so...

568
00:37:15,316 --> 00:37:16,693
I know.

569
00:37:17,777 --> 00:37:20,989
I wonder which lucky lady
will end up with our Minjae.

570
00:37:21,865 --> 00:37:24,284
If not in Korea,
maybe she's in the States?

571
00:37:24,367 --> 00:37:25,702
His soulmate, I mean.

572
00:37:25,785 --> 00:37:27,287
Maybe she's American?

573
00:37:27,370 --> 00:37:28,955
[Seohyun] Yeah, maybe.

574
00:37:29,038 --> 00:37:31,791
Or maybe she's nearby.

575
00:37:32,584 --> 00:37:34,919
[Seohyun laughs]

576
00:37:35,003 --> 00:37:36,212
[door closes]

577
00:37:40,508 --> 00:37:42,552
-[Seohyun] Looks like they cleaned up.
-[Minjae grunts]

578
00:37:44,888 --> 00:37:45,889
[sighs]

579
00:37:50,894 --> 00:37:53,772
I heard the school wedding hall
is really hard to book.

580
00:37:53,855 --> 00:37:55,190
-How did you manage to get it?
-[Seohyun scoffs]

581
00:37:55,273 --> 00:37:56,983
I've got my ways.

582
00:37:57,650 --> 00:37:59,986
I'll share them with you
when you get married.

583
00:38:04,157 --> 00:38:06,117
[Minjae]
No more late-night calls, I guess.

584
00:38:07,660 --> 00:38:11,206
No more calling each other up
to catch a movie on the weekend,

585
00:38:13,333 --> 00:38:18,296
or randomly taking off for the beach
on a freezing winter day.

586
00:38:21,007 --> 00:38:23,092
So, what, you're happy about it?

587
00:38:23,176 --> 00:38:24,844
You're saying it's a good thing?

588
00:38:24,928 --> 00:38:26,638
[Minjae] No, I'm saying...

589
00:38:26,721 --> 00:38:31,100
We're moving on
to the next chapter of our lives.

590
00:38:33,019 --> 00:38:34,020
[Seohyun] Minjae.

591
00:38:34,103 --> 00:38:35,104
[Minjae] Yes?

592
00:38:35,188 --> 00:38:37,649
Instead of a wedding gift,
I'd like to ask you a favor.

593
00:38:38,149 --> 00:38:39,192
[Minjae] What is it?

594
00:38:39,275 --> 00:38:40,944
Do you need anything?

595
00:38:41,653 --> 00:38:43,363
Could you sing at my wedding?

596
00:38:45,073 --> 00:38:47,200
-What? Sing at your wedding?
-[Seohyun] Yes, sing.

597
00:38:48,451 --> 00:38:52,622
[chuckles] Come on, you're a great singer.
You're the only one I can ask.

598
00:38:53,581 --> 00:38:54,624
Hey, wake up.

599
00:38:54,707 --> 00:38:57,335
This isn't karaoke after some work dinner.

600
00:38:57,418 --> 00:38:59,879
This is your wedding,
a once-in-a-lifetime event.

601
00:38:59,963 --> 00:39:01,631
Well, who knows?

602
00:39:01,714 --> 00:39:05,844
It could be once, it could be twice...
[snickers]

603
00:39:06,511 --> 00:39:08,680
Come on. Do it for me.

604
00:39:08,763 --> 00:39:09,764
[scoffs]

605
00:39:10,723 --> 00:39:13,017
Mr. Nam seriously needs his eyes checked.

606
00:39:13,643 --> 00:39:15,228
What does he even see in you?

607
00:39:15,311 --> 00:39:17,105
I feel so bad for the guy. I really do.

608
00:39:17,939 --> 00:39:20,191
[Seohyun] So you're not doing it?

609
00:39:21,067 --> 00:39:23,528
Of course not. I can't.

610
00:39:23,611 --> 00:39:25,280
Me? Sing at a wedding?

611
00:39:26,155 --> 00:39:27,657
Really? [sighs]

612
00:39:28,867 --> 00:39:30,618
Then I'll tell the guys.

613
00:39:30,702 --> 00:39:31,703
[Minjae] Tell them what?

614
00:39:32,328 --> 00:39:34,038
She seriously needs her eyes checked.

615
00:39:34,122 --> 00:39:36,332
What does she even see
in a loser like you?

616
00:39:37,542 --> 00:39:39,335
She's just young and naive

617
00:39:39,419 --> 00:39:42,338
and doesn't know how the world works,
am I right? [snickers]

618
00:39:43,047 --> 00:39:47,760
She has no clue how petty and obnoxious
our dear Park Minjae is.

619
00:39:47,844 --> 00:39:50,430
Imagine what that pretty girl
will have to go through.

620
00:39:50,513 --> 00:39:52,390
I already feel sorry for her.

621
00:39:52,473 --> 00:39:53,933
I really do.

622
00:39:54,017 --> 00:39:56,019
[♪ lively music playing]

623
00:39:57,270 --> 00:39:59,480
So are you going to sing or not?

624
00:40:03,443 --> 00:40:05,445
[♪ lively music continues playing]

625
00:40:41,940 --> 00:40:45,735
[doorbell rings]

626
00:41:11,678 --> 00:41:13,680
[♪ music fades]

627
00:41:42,709 --> 00:41:44,419
Wait, excuse me.

628
00:41:49,173 --> 00:41:50,174
Yes?

629
00:41:50,258 --> 00:41:51,634
Who are you?

630
00:41:52,802 --> 00:41:54,095
What do you mean, who am I?

631
00:41:54,846 --> 00:41:57,181
And who are you?

632
00:41:59,642 --> 00:42:02,228
I'm Park Minjae's girlfriend.

633
00:42:07,775 --> 00:42:09,777
[♪ piano music playing]

634
00:42:16,034 --> 00:42:17,076
Okay. Thank you.

635
00:42:17,160 --> 00:42:18,161
Thank you.

636
00:42:21,414 --> 00:42:22,498
Lim Youjin?

637
00:42:22,999 --> 00:42:24,000
[Youjin] Yes.

638
00:42:26,127 --> 00:42:27,879
Can I just call you Youjin?

639
00:42:27,962 --> 00:42:29,589
Or Ms. Youjin?

640
00:42:30,131 --> 00:42:32,091
Please, just call me Youjin.

641
00:42:32,884 --> 00:42:34,635
And feel free to be casual with me.

642
00:42:35,136 --> 00:42:38,723
[chuckles softly]
I will, once we get a little closer.

643
00:42:41,893 --> 00:42:45,605
Minjae never told me about his girlfriend,
so I was surprised.

644
00:42:55,448 --> 00:42:56,532
[softly] Thank you.

645
00:42:58,993 --> 00:43:01,287
[Eunjoo] So are you
in the same lab as him?

646
00:43:01,370 --> 00:43:02,789
At Seohan National University?

647
00:43:02,872 --> 00:43:03,873
Yes.

648
00:43:05,333 --> 00:43:08,169
It's so cool to see a woman
studying robotics.

649
00:43:08,252 --> 00:43:11,464
[chuckles softly] I'm just learning.

650
00:43:11,547 --> 00:43:13,091
I don't really know much yet.

651
00:43:13,841 --> 00:43:15,510
It's really cool.

652
00:43:15,593 --> 00:43:17,553
And you and Minjae look great together.

653
00:43:20,932 --> 00:43:24,227
Your parents must be so happy
to have a cool daughter like you.

654
00:43:25,144 --> 00:43:26,270
[chuckling] Not at all.

655
00:43:26,771 --> 00:43:28,189
What do your parents do?

656
00:43:29,649 --> 00:43:31,400
[Youjin]
They run a small auto repair shop.

657
00:43:32,276 --> 00:43:33,277
Pardon?

658
00:43:34,237 --> 00:43:35,446
An auto repair shop.

659
00:43:36,030 --> 00:43:38,157
Oh... For cars.

660
00:43:38,241 --> 00:43:40,409
Cars are machines too. [inhales]

661
00:43:40,493 --> 00:43:42,620
Looks like you inherited
your parents' talents.

662
00:43:45,123 --> 00:43:46,374
What about your mother?

663
00:43:46,457 --> 00:43:47,667
Is she a housewife?

664
00:43:47,750 --> 00:43:50,002
She works at the auto repair shop too.

665
00:43:51,254 --> 00:43:52,713
She's a mechanic too?

666
00:43:54,173 --> 00:43:55,716
She does the bookkeeping.

667
00:43:56,676 --> 00:43:59,303
She handles the receipts
and finances for the shop.

668
00:43:59,387 --> 00:44:03,099
Right. I thought she was a mechanic too.
You surprised me there.

669
00:44:03,724 --> 00:44:04,934
[chuckles]

670
00:44:07,562 --> 00:44:08,855
Do you have any siblings?

671
00:44:10,231 --> 00:44:12,191
I have a brother
who's a year older than me.

672
00:44:12,733 --> 00:44:14,277
[Eunjoo] A year older, that means...

673
00:44:14,819 --> 00:44:16,154
He's 26.

674
00:44:17,446 --> 00:44:18,781
He must be a student then.

675
00:44:20,241 --> 00:44:23,035
No, he works at the auto repair shop too.

676
00:44:26,539 --> 00:44:28,332
Your family sounds so close-knit.

677
00:44:29,625 --> 00:44:31,127
It's really lovely.

678
00:44:36,382 --> 00:44:38,342
[door lock chimes]

679
00:44:44,765 --> 00:44:45,766
[door lock chimes]

680
00:44:46,350 --> 00:44:47,351
Youjin.

681
00:45:03,743 --> 00:45:05,578
It was nice meeting you today.

682
00:45:05,661 --> 00:45:06,913
I had a great time.

683
00:45:07,455 --> 00:45:08,456
[Youjin] Sure.

684
00:45:10,291 --> 00:45:12,710
Uh... And I'd appreciate it

685
00:45:12,793 --> 00:45:15,254
if you didn't tell Minjae
that we met today.

686
00:45:17,590 --> 00:45:21,302
He's going to give me an earful
for meeting you without him.

687
00:45:22,011 --> 00:45:23,721
He's so bossy with me.

688
00:45:26,224 --> 00:45:28,601
Please don't tell Minjae.

689
00:45:28,684 --> 00:45:29,852
Can you do that for me?

690
00:45:30,519 --> 00:45:31,938
[chuckles softly] Okay.

691
00:45:32,897 --> 00:45:33,898
[Eunjoo] Thank you.

692
00:45:45,534 --> 00:45:48,829
Oh... Hop in. I'll drive you home.

693
00:45:48,913 --> 00:45:51,249
No, it's okay.
I can get home pretty quickly by bus.

694
00:45:51,332 --> 00:45:52,333
Your car's here.

695
00:45:53,417 --> 00:45:54,543
[Eunjoo] Do you live near here?

696
00:45:55,586 --> 00:45:56,587
Yes.

697
00:45:57,213 --> 00:45:58,506
Where do you live?

698
00:46:00,091 --> 00:46:01,133
Bongcheon-dong.

699
00:46:02,176 --> 00:46:05,471
Bongcheon-dong? Is the auto repair shop
in Bongcheon-dong too?

700
00:46:06,264 --> 00:46:07,265
Yes.

701
00:46:08,057 --> 00:46:09,892
What's the name of the auto repair shop?

702
00:46:10,977 --> 00:46:13,104
I'm just curious.

703
00:46:20,569 --> 00:46:21,821
[sighs]

704
00:46:30,830 --> 00:46:34,166
[cellphone vibrating]

705
00:46:43,092 --> 00:46:45,261
[clears throat] Hey.

706
00:46:46,304 --> 00:46:47,305
Where are you?

707
00:46:49,181 --> 00:46:51,183
[<i>♪ </i>soft music playing]

708
00:46:52,768 --> 00:46:54,103
I'm home too.

709
00:46:54,186 --> 00:46:56,689
My mom wanted me home early,
so I came back.

710
00:46:56,772 --> 00:46:57,773
Ah...

711
00:46:58,316 --> 00:47:00,318
Sorry I got home so late.

712
00:47:00,401 --> 00:47:02,611
You just did chores all day and left,
didn't you?

713
00:47:03,821 --> 00:47:04,822
[Youjin] Yeah.

714
00:47:07,408 --> 00:47:08,826
You can do them next time.

715
00:47:09,618 --> 00:47:10,786
We'll take turns.

716
00:47:11,287 --> 00:47:13,622
Okay. I'll make you
something good next time.

717
00:47:14,957 --> 00:47:16,042
Thanks for this.

718
00:47:17,877 --> 00:47:18,878
Bye.

719
00:47:20,838 --> 00:47:21,839
[line disconnects]

720
00:47:50,993 --> 00:47:54,330
CHEIL AUTO REPAIR SHOP

721
00:47:54,413 --> 00:47:56,457
Let's watch baseball, not the soap opera.

722
00:47:56,540 --> 00:47:57,583
It's almost over.

723
00:47:58,167 --> 00:47:59,210
Just wait.

724
00:48:02,630 --> 00:48:04,924
[woman on TV]<i> I've always wanted</i>
<i>to ask you this, Hyeri.</i>

725
00:48:08,511 --> 00:48:09,512
We got a car.

726
00:48:10,012 --> 00:48:11,013
Come on.

727
00:48:14,266 --> 00:48:15,267
[woman on TV] <i>Junil...</i>

728
00:48:20,689 --> 00:48:22,566
-[Youseong] Hello. Welcome!
-[Yongseok] Welcome.

729
00:48:22,650 --> 00:48:23,651
Hello.

730
00:48:28,364 --> 00:48:30,866
The brakes aren't working right.
Could you take a look?

731
00:48:30,950 --> 00:48:31,951
[Yongseok] Sure.

732
00:48:32,034 --> 00:48:33,369
-[Youseong] Is your car key inside?
-Yes.

733
00:48:33,452 --> 00:48:34,829
-[Youseong] Please wait inside.
-This way.

734
00:48:34,912 --> 00:48:35,913
Okay.

735
00:48:41,585 --> 00:48:43,003
[Miyoung chuckles]

736
00:48:43,087 --> 00:48:44,713
Hello, please have a seat here.

737
00:48:44,797 --> 00:48:45,798
Okay.

738
00:48:47,299 --> 00:48:49,009
[Miyoung]
Would you like something to drink?

739
00:48:49,093 --> 00:48:50,886
Yeah, sure. Anything's fine.

740
00:48:50,970 --> 00:48:51,971
[Miyoung] Okay.

741
00:48:57,476 --> 00:48:59,311
Is this your first time at our shop?

742
00:48:59,395 --> 00:49:00,396
Yes.

743
00:49:01,105 --> 00:49:03,274
[Miyoung] You don't seem to be
from around here.

744
00:49:04,984 --> 00:49:08,654
We don't get many Mercedes owners
in this neighborhood.

745
00:49:10,573 --> 00:49:12,783
We haven't worked on that many Mercedes,

746
00:49:13,492 --> 00:49:15,911
but we've done this a long time,
so we know our stuff.

747
00:49:15,995 --> 00:49:17,913
-Thank you.
-[Miyoung] Sure.

748
00:49:23,252 --> 00:49:24,253
[slurps]

749
00:49:27,381 --> 00:49:30,468
Looks like your brake pads
are a bit worn down.

750
00:49:30,551 --> 00:49:32,386
Once replaced, you should be good to go.

751
00:49:33,137 --> 00:49:34,346
Then please go ahead.

752
00:49:34,430 --> 00:49:38,392
Well, the thing is, we don't have
the Mercedes parts in stock right now.

753
00:49:38,476 --> 00:49:40,769
You should take it
to an authorized service center.

754
00:49:42,271 --> 00:49:44,023
Ah... Really?

755
00:49:44,607 --> 00:49:46,025
Well, I guess I have no choice.

756
00:49:46,108 --> 00:49:47,943
Gosh, I'm sorry I can't help.

757
00:49:48,027 --> 00:49:49,528
No. Don't worry.

758
00:49:51,822 --> 00:49:52,865
We're sorry.

759
00:49:52,948 --> 00:49:54,617
-[Eunjoo] That's all right.
-Okay.

760
00:50:01,123 --> 00:50:02,124
[grunts]

761
00:50:04,251 --> 00:50:05,252
[door opens]

762
00:50:08,881 --> 00:50:10,049
Mom?

763
00:50:10,132 --> 00:50:11,926
[Miyoung] Yes. You were home.

764
00:50:17,723 --> 00:50:19,892
-What's that?
-[Miyoung] Ah...

765
00:50:20,392 --> 00:50:22,770
This woman came into the shop today.

766
00:50:23,771 --> 00:50:26,482
She looked so elegant,
and her skin was just glowing.

767
00:50:27,024 --> 00:50:30,277
You could tell right away she was
some wealthy lady. Like really rich.

768
00:50:30,819 --> 00:50:32,863
She even pulled up
in a white Mercedes. [gasps]

769
00:50:33,489 --> 00:50:35,616
Wow. [chuckles]

770
00:50:35,699 --> 00:50:39,662
But we didn't have any Mercedes parts,
so we told her we couldn't fix it.

771
00:50:39,745 --> 00:50:42,623
Then she apologized
for putting us through all that trouble

772
00:50:42,706 --> 00:50:44,708
and said we should at least accept this.

773
00:50:44,792 --> 00:50:45,960
Gosh.

774
00:50:46,043 --> 00:50:49,505
How could someone
be so polite and considerate?

775
00:50:49,588 --> 00:50:51,757
Still, you shouldn't accept
something like this.

776
00:50:51,840 --> 00:50:53,634
I tried to say no at first.

777
00:50:53,717 --> 00:50:57,680
But then she said she'd received it
as a gift herself,

778
00:50:57,763 --> 00:51:00,599
and there weren't enough people
in her family to finish it all,

779
00:51:00,683 --> 00:51:02,017
so it would just go bad.

780
00:51:03,602 --> 00:51:06,438
She gave it to us because it'd go bad?
What are we, beggars?

781
00:51:06,522 --> 00:51:08,190
What do you mean, beggars?

782
00:51:09,149 --> 00:51:10,901
[Youjin]
You still shouldn't have accepted it.

783
00:51:10,985 --> 00:51:13,028
What do you think she'll think of us?

784
00:51:13,112 --> 00:51:14,822
She gave it to us as an apology.

785
00:51:14,905 --> 00:51:17,324
Who gives something like this
as an apology?

786
00:51:18,367 --> 00:51:21,620
Stop watching those soap operas all day
and read a book once in a while.

787
00:51:21,704 --> 00:51:23,956
Use your brain for once
and get some common sense.

788
00:51:24,665 --> 00:51:26,834
No wonder you bring home stuff
like some beggar.

789
00:51:26,917 --> 00:51:28,502
Don't you have any pride, Mom?

790
00:51:30,838 --> 00:51:32,548
God, seriously.

791
00:51:32,631 --> 00:51:34,633
[Youjin breathing heavily]

792
00:51:40,222 --> 00:51:41,890
-[Miyoung sobs]
-[Youjin sighs]

793
00:51:41,974 --> 00:51:43,976
[whimpering]

794
00:51:44,059 --> 00:51:46,061
[♪ emotional music playing]

795
00:51:56,322 --> 00:51:58,324
[sniffing, sobbing]

796
00:52:20,304 --> 00:52:21,305
[Miyoung sniffles]

797
00:52:39,823 --> 00:52:40,824
Mom.

798
00:52:41,784 --> 00:52:43,202
Mom, I'm sorry.

799
00:52:44,328 --> 00:52:46,163
Mom, I was wrong. [sobs]

800
00:52:46,246 --> 00:52:47,581
Mom, I'm sorry.

801
00:52:47,665 --> 00:52:49,500
Mom, I'm sorry. [crying]

802
00:52:49,583 --> 00:52:50,959
I was wrong.

803
00:52:53,337 --> 00:52:55,214
Mom. [crying]

804
00:52:57,925 --> 00:52:59,635
Mom, I'm sorry.

805
00:53:03,222 --> 00:53:04,348
Mom, I'm sorry.

806
00:53:09,937 --> 00:53:11,355
[Miyoung] No, I'm sorry.

807
00:53:19,113 --> 00:53:21,115
[♪ music fades]

808
00:53:22,199 --> 00:53:24,410
TWO PEOPLE

809
00:53:24,493 --> 00:53:28,080
[Minjae singing] ♪ <i>After a long day </i>♪

810
00:53:28,956 --> 00:53:31,792
♪ <i>Two people beneath the moonlight </i>♪

811
00:53:32,459 --> 00:53:33,669
[in normal voice] Is this right?

812
00:53:35,963 --> 00:53:38,173
This... And...

813
00:53:40,050 --> 00:53:42,177
PLEDGE OF LOVE

814
00:53:42,261 --> 00:53:48,183
[singing] ♪ <i>The moment I've longed for </i>♪

815
00:53:49,184 --> 00:53:50,185
[sighs]

816
00:53:56,191 --> 00:53:59,570
-[line connects, rings]
-[Youjin sighs]

817
00:53:59,653 --> 00:54:01,613
I think anything would be fine.

818
00:54:02,781 --> 00:54:04,616
I don't know much about music.

819
00:54:04,700 --> 00:54:06,243
[Minjae] <i>Come on.</i>

820
00:54:06,326 --> 00:54:09,955
<i>There must be a song you like.</i>

821
00:54:10,038 --> 00:54:12,624
Or something you'd want to hear.

822
00:54:12,708 --> 00:54:15,169
If you can think of one,
I'll sing it for you.

823
00:54:15,252 --> 00:54:16,670
[♪ gentle music playing]

824
00:54:16,754 --> 00:54:18,922
If you sing at night,
ghosts will come out.

825
00:54:20,340 --> 00:54:21,759
[Minjae] <i>Wasn't it snakes?</i>

826
00:54:21,842 --> 00:54:24,344
The thing that comes out
if you sing at night. Snakes.

827
00:54:25,929 --> 00:54:27,473
[Youjin] <i>That's what the flute does.</i>

828
00:54:28,307 --> 00:54:30,100
If you play the flute, snakes come out.

829
00:54:30,184 --> 00:54:31,560
If you sing, ghosts come out.

830
00:54:32,311 --> 00:54:34,146
What happened to your voice, by the way?

831
00:54:34,938 --> 00:54:36,106
Are you feeling unwell?

832
00:54:36,648 --> 00:54:37,649
Are you sick?

833
00:54:38,192 --> 00:54:40,277
No, I'm not.

834
00:54:40,360 --> 00:54:41,487
I'm fine.

835
00:54:43,363 --> 00:54:46,575
[sighs] Just sing something old.
Something classic.

836
00:54:47,743 --> 00:54:49,453
Okay.

837
00:54:49,536 --> 00:54:51,997
I'll do more research.

838
00:54:52,664 --> 00:54:53,665
Okay.

839
00:54:54,500 --> 00:54:55,501
Bye.

840
00:54:57,794 --> 00:54:58,795
[line disconnects]

841
00:55:03,967 --> 00:55:05,969
[breathes heavily]

842
00:55:11,808 --> 00:55:13,810
[♪ music fades]

843
00:55:22,152 --> 00:55:24,154
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY
FACULTY CLUB

844
00:55:24,238 --> 00:55:26,240
-[indistinct chatter]
-[<i>♪ </i>lively instrumental music playing]

845
00:55:32,996 --> 00:55:35,707
[photographer] I'm going
to take the picture now. Look this way.

846
00:55:35,791 --> 00:55:37,459
All right, one, two, three.

847
00:55:37,543 --> 00:55:38,544
One, two, three.

848
00:55:38,627 --> 00:55:40,462
-One, two, three.
-Look over here.

849
00:55:41,463 --> 00:55:42,589
Thank you.

850
00:55:42,673 --> 00:55:44,258
-Congratulations, Seohyun.
-Thanks.

851
00:55:44,341 --> 00:55:46,510
[Youjin] Yeah. And? Did you get it?

852
00:55:48,136 --> 00:55:50,347
Thanks, Subin. You're the best. Bye.

853
00:55:53,267 --> 00:55:54,351
-[Seohyun] Thanks, Auntie.
-Okay.

854
00:55:54,434 --> 00:55:56,436
-[Seoyhun] Make sure to enjoy the meal.
-See you later.

855
00:55:56,520 --> 00:55:58,522
-Say bye to your aunt. [chuckles]
-Bye, Auntie.

856
00:55:59,314 --> 00:56:00,941
Your bouquet is almost here.

857
00:56:01,024 --> 00:56:02,693
That's great to hear. Thank you.

858
00:56:03,819 --> 00:56:05,737
[coordinator] Seohyun,
let's get ready for your entrance.

859
00:56:05,821 --> 00:56:06,822
Okay.

860
00:56:06,905 --> 00:56:07,906
[crowd clapping]

861
00:56:07,990 --> 00:56:11,076
[host]<i> Next, we will have the ceremonial</i>
<i>candle lighting to light the way</i>

862
00:56:11,159 --> 00:56:13,412
for the bride and groom's bright future.

863
00:56:20,168 --> 00:56:21,169
Light the candles.

864
00:56:24,006 --> 00:56:28,218
[♪ grand music playing]

865
00:56:34,766 --> 00:56:35,767
[Subin] Youjin!

866
00:56:35,851 --> 00:56:37,519
-Here.
-Subin. Thanks so much.

867
00:56:38,979 --> 00:56:40,564
Seohyun, here.

868
00:56:40,647 --> 00:56:43,650
-Oh! Thank you.
-Wishing you a happy marriage!

869
00:56:43,734 --> 00:56:45,152
[Seohyun] Thank you. We got this!

870
00:56:46,361 --> 00:56:50,157
[host] It's time for the stars of today's
celebration to make their entrance.

871
00:56:50,240 --> 00:56:53,452
They met at the same company
as a researcher and a team leader,

872
00:56:53,535 --> 00:56:58,165
and now they've promised
to become a team for life.

873
00:56:58,248 --> 00:57:03,462
As they take the first step
on their long journey together,

874
00:57:03,545 --> 00:57:08,133
please greet them
with your loudest cheers and applause.

875
00:57:08,216 --> 00:57:10,344
Please welcome the bride and groom!

876
00:57:10,427 --> 00:57:12,429
-[♪ lively music playing]
-[applause]

877
00:57:39,206 --> 00:57:41,208
[♪ music fades]

878
00:57:41,291 --> 00:57:43,919
[applauding, cheering]

879
00:57:44,002 --> 00:57:50,592
Next, the couple will exchange rings
as a symbol of their love.

880
00:57:50,676 --> 00:57:56,098
Groom, please place the ring
on the bride's finger,

881
00:57:56,181 --> 00:58:01,019
and bride, please place the ring
on the groom's.

882
00:58:07,317 --> 00:58:11,071
Next, the couple
will exchange wedding vows,

883
00:58:11,154 --> 00:58:13,156
committing themselves
to each other for life.

884
00:58:14,116 --> 00:58:18,370
We ask everyone here to bear witness

885
00:58:18,453 --> 00:58:22,040
as they recite their promises of love.

886
00:58:22,958 --> 00:58:24,459
[Yoonsoo] "Wedding Vow."

887
00:58:25,043 --> 00:58:26,169
[♪ gentle music playing]

888
00:58:26,253 --> 00:58:28,630
"When I think of our future together,

889
00:58:28,714 --> 00:58:32,592
the first thing I picture is a life
filled with warmth and happiness.

890
00:58:32,676 --> 00:58:34,302
But I also know that the road ahead

891
00:58:34,386 --> 00:58:36,972
won't always be easy
or filled only with good times."

892
00:58:37,806 --> 00:58:40,183
[Yoonsoo] "Difficult moments will come,

893
00:58:40,267 --> 00:58:43,603
but just as we have until now,
we will face them hand in hand,

894
00:58:43,687 --> 00:58:46,356
trusting and cherishing one another."

895
00:58:47,023 --> 00:58:49,067
"We will always put each other first,

896
00:58:49,151 --> 00:58:51,737
express our love and gratitude
without holding back,

897
00:58:51,820 --> 00:58:53,739
and build a loving life together."

898
00:58:54,489 --> 00:58:58,076
[both] "Before everyone gathered here
today, we sincerely vow to love each other

899
00:58:58,160 --> 00:59:01,913
for all the years to come
just as we do in this moment,

900
00:59:01,997 --> 00:59:05,792
and to be the best friend
either of us could ever ask for."

901
00:59:05,876 --> 00:59:07,919
"Groom Nam Yoonsoo."

902
00:59:08,003 --> 00:59:09,838
"Bride Cha Seohyun."

903
00:59:09,921 --> 00:59:11,798
[host] <i>Please give them</i>
<i>a big round of applause.</i>

904
00:59:11,882 --> 00:59:13,884
[applauding]

905
00:59:18,972 --> 00:59:22,934
Next, we have a special song
for the bride and groom.

906
00:59:23,643 --> 00:59:29,691
It will be performed by the bride's
longtime friend, Park Minjae.

907
00:59:29,775 --> 00:59:31,985
[all applauding]

908
00:59:35,030 --> 00:59:36,823
[♪ piano music playing,
Kim Kwangjin "Pledge of Love"]

909
01:00:03,058 --> 01:00:08,230
[singing] ♪ <i>The moment I've longed for </i>♪

910
01:00:09,773 --> 01:00:15,362
♪ <i>Is finally here </i>♪

911
01:00:16,279 --> 01:00:22,619
♪ <i>With everyone's blessings </i>♪

912
01:00:23,537 --> 01:00:29,084
♪ <i>We're making our vows of love </i>♪

913
01:00:30,335 --> 01:00:35,674
♪ <i>When the years have passed </i>♪

914
01:00:36,967 --> 01:00:42,514
♪ <i>And we're weary and ill </i>♪

915
01:00:43,181 --> 01:00:49,312
♪ <i>Will we still stand by each other </i>♪

916
01:00:50,230 --> 01:00:55,694
♪ <i>And offer comfort, just as we do now? </i>♪

917
01:00:55,777 --> 01:01:02,117
♪ <i>With all the years we have </i>♪

918
01:01:02,200 --> 01:01:08,164
♪ <i>Yet to walk through together </i>♪

919
01:01:08,248 --> 01:01:15,046
♪ <i>Do you believe the promises </i>♪

920
01:01:15,130 --> 01:01:21,887
♪ <i>We've made will never change? </i>♪

921
01:01:22,012 --> 01:01:28,143
♪ <i>There will be difficult days </i>♪

922
01:01:28,310 --> 01:01:34,357
♪ <i>But I know I will have no regrets </i>♪

923
01:01:34,441 --> 01:01:38,570
♪ <i>I believe our lives </i>♪

924
01:01:38,653 --> 01:01:43,658
♪ <i>Will be filled with love </i>♪

925
01:01:43,742 --> 01:01:50,749
♪ <i>Until the day heaven calls us home </i>♪

926
01:02:10,226 --> 01:02:11,227
[Minjae in normal voice] Hey.

927
01:02:15,774 --> 01:02:16,942
I love you.

928
01:02:18,652 --> 01:02:20,028
Do you love me too?

929
01:02:20,904 --> 01:02:22,948
Why would you ask me all of a sudden?

930
01:02:24,407 --> 01:02:26,368
You love me at least a little, right?

931
01:02:26,868 --> 01:02:28,828
Probably not as much
as my mom does, though.

932
01:02:31,164 --> 01:02:35,835
No one in the world
loves me as much as she does.

933
01:02:37,671 --> 01:02:38,797
So...

934
01:02:40,757 --> 01:02:44,177
if anyone messes with or hurts my mom
or anyone else in my family,

935
01:02:45,387 --> 01:02:46,721
I will never let that slide.

936
01:02:50,433 --> 01:02:51,893
But that's a different story.

937
01:02:51,977 --> 01:02:53,478
You didn't do anything wrong.

938
01:02:54,604 --> 01:02:55,605
What?

939
01:02:58,733 --> 01:03:01,069
I got to be with someone
far too good for me,

940
01:03:02,696 --> 01:03:06,116
so even if I have to suffer
or be punished for it someday,

941
01:03:06,658 --> 01:03:08,702
I don't care. So be it.

942
01:03:19,421 --> 01:03:20,964
Park Minjae is mine.

943
01:03:22,799 --> 01:03:24,926
I'm never letting anyone
take you away from me.

944
01:03:27,095 --> 01:03:28,471
You're mine.

945
01:03:29,597 --> 01:03:31,349
No one can ever take you away from me.

946
01:03:35,020 --> 01:03:36,396
Have you been drinking?

947
01:03:36,479 --> 01:03:39,399
No. I didn't. I'm completely sober.

948
01:03:41,067 --> 01:03:42,068
[Minjae chuckles softly]

949
01:03:45,822 --> 01:03:47,115
I love you.

950
01:03:47,198 --> 01:03:49,200
[♪ music fades]

951
01:03:52,579 --> 01:03:53,955
[mouthing] Me too.

952
01:03:55,790 --> 01:03:57,083
-Hmm?
-[Minjae] Hmm?

953
01:03:57,167 --> 01:03:58,960
[♪ gentle music builds]

954
01:03:59,044 --> 01:04:00,628
If you didn't hear it, never mind.

955
01:04:02,464 --> 01:04:03,465
I did.

956
01:04:06,426 --> 01:04:07,427
I love you.

957
01:04:12,849 --> 01:04:13,850
Me too.

958
01:04:28,323 --> 01:04:33,244
BETWEEN STEPS

959
01:04:33,328 --> 01:04:35,330
[♪ lively music playing]

960
01:05:09,364 --> 01:05:10,365
Turn a bit this way.

961
01:05:10,448 --> 01:05:12,117
<i>I don't think you like me that much.</i>

962
01:05:12,200 --> 01:05:13,201
-Hello.
-[Minjae] Yes.

963
01:05:13,284 --> 01:05:14,661
[Sejin] <i>Isn't she ridiculously pretty?</i>

964
01:05:14,744 --> 01:05:16,704
I can't believe she's Lim Youjin's friend.

965
01:05:17,664 --> 01:05:20,500
And you'd still save Subin over me?

966
01:05:20,583 --> 01:05:24,129
But how could I set her up
with that nutjob Kim Sejin?

967
01:05:24,212 --> 01:05:25,755
What? What are you doing here?

968
01:05:25,839 --> 01:05:29,342
[Sejin] <i>I don't know why you're trying</i>
<i>to get close with Minjae,</i>

969
01:05:29,425 --> 01:05:32,929
but he's a completely different
kind of person from you.

970
01:05:33,012 --> 01:05:34,722
Let's save that kiss for home.

971
01:05:34,806 --> 01:05:35,807
You're cute.
